---
<p>Go and Bayan share small languages, plain code, fast builds and one way to format. Bayan checks differently: no <code>nil</code>, no <code>if err != nil</code>, no pointers, and no interface satisfied by accident.</p>
<p>Every program ran with the compiler; the output is real.</p>

<h2 id="table">Common tasks side by side</h2>
